WEBVTT

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:03.400
A probability compares favourable outcomes with all

00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:06.630
outcomes, but only if the outcomes are equally likely.

00:00:07.200 --> 00:00:09.750
A bag holds two red counters and one blue.

00:00:10.320 --> 00:00:12.440
There are two colours, but red is not a one

00:00:12.440 --> 00:00:13.150
in two chance.

00:00:13.760 --> 00:00:16.210
There are three counters, each equally likely,

00:00:16.700 --> 00:00:17.910
and two of them are red.

00:00:18.840 --> 00:00:21.500
Counting names instead of real outcomes is the most

00:00:21.500 --> 00:00:22.990
common probability mistake.

00:00:23.520 --> 00:00:26.200
The fix is to list outcomes that genuinely are equally

00:00:26.200 --> 00:00:27.670
likely, then count.

00:00:28.610 --> 00:00:31.710
Toss two fair coins separately, so one result cannot

00:00:31.710 --> 00:00:32.620
affect the other.

00:00:33.190 --> 00:00:35.740
What is the probability of getting exactly one head?

00:00:36.190 --> 00:00:38.680
Someone says there are three results, two heads,

00:00:38.930 --> 00:00:41.820
one head or no heads, so the answer is one third.

00:00:42.590 --> 00:00:44.380
Pause and decide whether that is right.

00:00:48.100 --> 00:00:51.190
Give the coins names: first coin and second coin.

00:00:51.720 --> 00:00:54.450
Now there are four outcomes: head head, head tail,

00:00:54.720 --> 00:00:56.070
tail head, and tail tail.

00:00:56.560 --> 00:00:58.210
These four are equally likely.

00:00:59.150 --> 00:01:02.340
Exactly one head happens in two of the four: head tail,

00:01:02.570 --> 00:01:03.280
and tail head.

00:01:03.970 --> 00:01:06.750
So the probability is two out of four, which is one

00:01:06.750 --> 00:01:08.320
half, not one third.

00:01:08.850 --> 00:01:10.710
The three results in the earlier list were

00:01:10.710 --> 00:01:11.840
not equally likely.

00:01:12.750 --> 00:01:14.500
Roll two fair dice separately.

00:01:15.150 --> 00:01:17.420
There are thirty-six equally likely pairs.

00:01:18.170 --> 00:01:20.360
A total of seven comes from six of them,

00:01:20.490 --> 00:01:24.330
so its probability is six out of thirty-six, one sixth.

00:01:24.330 --> 00:01:27.240
A total of two comes from only one pair.

00:01:27.710 --> 00:01:30.740
The totals are not equally likely, but the pairs are.

00:01:31.620 --> 00:01:34.090
Label the objects so each outcome is visible.

00:01:34.620 --> 00:01:36.330
Check the outcomes are equally likely.

00:01:36.740 --> 00:01:38.330
Then count favourable out of total.

00:01:38.900 --> 00:01:40.930
Notebook challenge: two dice are rolled.

00:01:41.660 --> 00:01:43.320
What is the probability that the two numbers

00:01:43.320 --> 00:01:44.050
are the same?
